{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings","id":1181627,"title":"Flexible magic system for changelings?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-02T05:29:44-08:00","id":1181627,"title":"Flexible magic system for changelings?","content":"I love Changeling: The Lost but I was always a little disappointed that there wasn\u2019t a more flexible magic system. In Dark ages: Fae there was unleashing, which I thought was pretty cool and there are a few homebrew systems but they never really clicked with me. Do you guys have any ideas for this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23780-overlord62","user":"Overlord62","date":". 02-02-2018, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23780-overlord62","name":"Overlord62","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T06:34:53-08:00","id":1181635,"title":"","content":"You're talking about essentially a sorcery system for fae creatures? One thing you could do is use hedge magic (lowercase &quot;H&quot;) as a model for this. If Changelings cannot stack supernatural merits then use a Contract to simulate the ability to do basic magic, blessings, curses and the like. <br /> <br /> I think one reason nothing has been floated, however, is because Changelings and their power source seem tied up in the mechanisms for agreements and bargains with the universe. So while a given Changeling can work a great deal of 'sorcery' they do it through the defined pathways that they discover (Contracts).<br /> <br /> And then there's simple word-count....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf (who is not an expert)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T06:42:31-08:00","id":1181636,"title":"","content":"Could you please provide links to all the systems you've seen and explain what you didn't like about them? Otherwise, it's gonna be very hard to divine what you are looking for? <br /> <br /> Like, what do you mean by flexible magic system? Something like the ability to basically perform any magical act you can think of (within general CoD level limits) with the appropriate mystical ritual? <br /> <br /> I would argue that Changelings already have more flexible array of powers than Werewolves and Vampires fluffwise. Sure, there's homebrew powers for both, but Werewolf Gifts are all supposed to be focused on making you a better hunter and Changelings are in-universe supposed to be able to bargain with all sorts of crazy things to get new Contracts, meaning that piling your PCs and NPCs up with Homebrew Contracts is more justified than it is for Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T07:11:05-08:00","id":1181646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181636#post1181636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you please provide links to all the systems you've seen and explain what you didn't like about them? Otherwise, it's gonna be very hard to divine what you are looking for? <br /> <br /> Like, what do you mean by flexible magic system? Something like the ability to basically perform any magical act you can think of (within general CoD level limits) with the appropriate mystical ritual? <br /> <br /> I would argue that Changelings already have more flexible array of powers than Werewolves and Vampires fluffwise. Sure, there's homebrew powers for both, but Werewolf Gifts are all supposed to be focused on making you a better hunter and Changelings are in-universe supposed to be able to bargain with all sorts of crazy things to get new Contracts, meaning that piling your PCs and NPCs up with Homebrew Contracts is more justified than it is for Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, first there\u2019s wyrd-sorcery which I felt was messy and unwieldy then there\u2019s wyrd-binding and I like the concept for it but it never really resonated with me. Also, by \u201cflexible magic system\u201d I mean something that emphasizes the chaotic nature of fae creatures. That\u2019s why I like the concept of Dark age: Fae\u2019s unleashing although the system could certainly use a few modifications.<br /> <br /> Edit: how do I post links?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23780-overlord62","name":"Overlord62","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T07:28:38-08:00","id":1181652,"title":"","content":"Press the symbol that looks like <u>A</u> and you get lots of options.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, what's Dark Age: Fae? If it's C:tD thing, I'd like to remind you that there's a big thematic difference between OWoD and NWoD Fae. OWoD fae are all about creativity and wonder. NWoD Fae (at least True Fae and arguably Changelings) borrow and steal all their ideas from mortals (even the Hedge denizens of 2e seem to be either from Ironside originally or descendants of Ironside creatures). Otherwise, they are creatively sterile. So I almost kind of wonder if there even is any thematic space for a flexible magic system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 02-02-2018, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T08:28:02-08:00","id":1181665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181652#post1181652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Press the symbol that looks like <u>A</u> and you get lots of options.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, what's Dark Age: Fae? If it's C:tD thing, I'd like to remind you that there's a big thematic difference between OWoD and NWoD Fae. OWoD fae are all about creativity and wonder. NWoD Fae (at least True Fae and arguably Changelings) borrow and steal all their ideas from mortals (even the Hedge denizens of 2e seem to be either from Ironside originally or descendants of Ironside creatures). Otherwise, they are creatively sterile. So I almost kind of wonder if there even is any thematic space for a flexible magic system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Also DA:F is actually very different from C:TD although it does use a few of the same terms. In DA:F the fae aren\u2019t born from human wonder and imagination but are actually raw, primordial magic made flesh. Magic was divided into Dawn, Day, Dusk and Night based on it\u2019s thematic effects. You could use cantrips, which were basically the same as contracts, or you could take a chunk of raw magic and unleash it. Unleashing was powerful and flexible but it had lot of ways it could go horribly wrong and I like that element of chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23780-overlord62","name":"Overlord62","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T08:31:28-08:00","id":1181667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overlord62</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181665#post1181665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks! Also DA:F is actually very different from C:TD although it does use a few of the same terms. In DA:F the fae aren\u2019t born from human wonder and imagination but are actually raw, primordial magic made flesh. Magic was divided into Dawn, Day, Dusk and Night based on it\u2019s thematic effects. You could use cantrips, which were basically the same as contracts, or you could take a chunk of raw magic and unleash it. Unleashing was powerful and flexible but it had lot of ways it could go horribly wrong and I like that element of chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like Mage and/or Talespinning with a really wild GM<br /> <br /> &quot;Raw Primordial made flesh&quot; almost sounds like Supernal Cryptids<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ok, still not sure whether DA:F is set in the OWoD or the NWoD or some other setting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 02-02-2018, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T09:23:00-08:00","id":1181683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181667#post1181667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: Ok, still not sure whether DA:F is set in the OWoD or the NWoD or some other setting</div> </div> </div> </div>It is OWoD ( just WoD now), but each game in WoD has very different cosmologies from each other. DA:F is essentially a different take on the idea of Changeling than either CtD or CtL (although it was before CtL). It was similar to but distinct from CtD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T09:50:54-08:00","id":1181691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181683#post1181683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is OWoD ( just WoD now), but each game in WoD has very different cosmologies from each other. DA:F is essentially a different take on the idea of Changeling than either CtD or CtL (although it was before CtL). It was similar to but distinct from CtD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this, part of the reason I like DA:F is that it got rid of a lot of things about C:tD that I hated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23780-overlord62","name":"Overlord62","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T10:18:18-08:00","id":1181701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overlord62</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings#post1181627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Changeling: The Lost but I was always a little disappointed that there wasn\u2019t a more flexible magic system. In Dark ages: Fae there was unleashing, which I thought was pretty cool and there are a few homebrew systems but they never really clicked with me. Do you guys have any ideas for this?</div> </div> </div> </div> Dreameaving and Hedgespinning are basically the free form types of Changeling magic, problem is most, but not all of their effects are limited to the Hedge or Dreams. Perhaps a future contract will allow their use elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Some contracts can be very flexible in use, with some creativity, to be almost restricted free forn magic, like the ability to grant objects a Mask (I forget the name) or Loyal Servant and Discreet Conjuration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T10:48:39-08:00","id":1181711,"title":"","content":"Sealing can function as very minor flexible magic giving sealing breakers any minor curse you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T11:01:11-08:00","id":1181715,"title":"","content":"Not sure if i said it before, but a big theme of 2e that i really like is that Changelings are hunted fugitives who have to beg, con and bargain for every little edge they can get. Thats why im not sure a flexible magic system is appropriate, at least at lower power levels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T11:04:47-08:00","id":1181717,"title":"","content":"It could be in theme with changeling if the magic system used is sortof like magic but put together with duck tape. Potentially strong but horribly unreliable. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T11:06:05-08:00","id":1181718,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1073308-homebrew-sorcery-rites?p=1178519#post1178519\">One thing</a> I've been playing around with (at least in the context of Fairy Tales), is to make various odd-ball effects Closed Rites/Rituals (from the Sorcery system in the Dark Eras Companion).<br /> <br /> Basically decide what you want the Rite to do, then come up with (about) 3 things doing it successfully requires. Spending a point of Fuel Stat (Glamour, in this case) means you can skip or reduce one of the elements, or improve the effect in some way.<br /> <br /> They are designed for mortals, in general, but you can pay-gate all kinds of features behind that optional cost.<br /> <br /> If you want, let Changelings come up with &quot;new&quot; Rites Ad Hoc. I'd borrow from some kind of narrative device or story to give it some structure, or you could roll dice against a chart of flexible options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-02-2018, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T14:10:23-08:00","id":1181792,"title":"","content":"One minor hack I'm planning to use that makes things a tad more flexible: making contract blessings something that applies on an individual level instead of by seeming. Any time you purchase a Favored Regalia contract you get one free blessing, which can either be one of the suggested ones or something new you homebrew with the ST. <br /> <br /> So like, if you're a light elemental who wants to throw blinding daggers and doesn't have dots in intimidate you can take the suggested &quot;darkling&quot; blessing when you get Elemental Weapon. Or as a Ogre with Sword as a Favored Regalia (or just one who spent extra exp) you can say &quot;Hey I'd like for my attacks to inflict Knockdown whenever I use this.&quot;<br /> <br /> Think of it like signing a lease. You have your standard terms and conditions, but if you're a relative (metaphorically representing Favored Regalia) they'll give you a discount and throw in a free dishwasher, or something like that. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T14:14:21-08:00","id":1181794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181717#post1181717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">magic but put together with duck tape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sin-eater Ceremonies<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181717#post1181717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potentially strong but horribly unreliable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage in a crowd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T15:58:45-08:00","id":1181833,"title":"","content":"I think the largest potential issue is that with a super wide magic system, it minimizes on the &quot;Bargaining&quot; aspect of Changeling if you can just get any sort of magical effect without having to make deals to get like a goblin contractor or something for it. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EioGQle5FQ14d3AIXGAXJA8AXbANuj-vwdgQS84eub4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">So could just take the Goblin Vow system from David Hill's 2e Changeling</a>?<br /> <br /> Make deals with nearby aspects of reality for temporary powers or boons. It's very flexible and able to provide many different abilities while still having the player act like a changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T16:28:59-08:00","id":1181843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181833#post1181833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the largest potential issue is that with a super wide magic system, it minimizes on the &amp;quot;Bargaining&amp;quot; aspect of Changeling if you can just get any sort of magical effect without having to make deals to get like a goblin contractor or something for it. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EioGQle5FQ14d3AIXGAXJA8AXbANuj-vwdgQS84eub4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">So could just take the Goblin Vow system from David Hill's 2e Changeling</a>?<br /> <br /> Make deals with nearby aspects of reality for temporary powers or boons. It's very flexible and able to provide many different abilities while still having the player act like a changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good to me. Expand it to various Contract-like effects (as in focus on tricksiness rather than direct power) and it would be perfect, though now that contracts are no longer dot-rated, you'd have to figure out how to balance which level of favors get which contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T16:43:50-08:00","id":1181848,"title":"","content":"You know, while we\u2019re on the subject of changeling magic, I had this idea for two new merits called Hedge-speak and Wyrd-script. They would basically function like Mage\u2019s runes and high speach and provide bonuses to contracts like making them more powerful or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23780-overlord62","name":"Overlord62","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T17:44:27-08:00","id":1181866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overlord62</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181848#post1181848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, while we\u2019re on the subject of changeling magic, I had this idea for two new merits called Hedge-speak and Wyrd-script. They would basically function like Mage\u2019s runes and high speach and provide bonuses to contracts like making them more powerful or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That frankly gets into design space that 1e directly recommended against for Contract design \u2014 specifically-occult-flavored secret words and magic runes are not the stuff of generalized fae abilities.<br /> <br /> As it stands the most flexible system of magic available to changelings is becoming a Hedge Denizen and picking up a long list of Goblin Contracts to trade out on the daily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T19:24:32-08:00","id":1181889,"title":"","content":"Think of it this way. Mages are scholarly imperious high magic, Vampires are horrific blood magic, Werewolves are brutal animist magic, Beasts are primal fear magic, Demons are reality-bending technomagic; Sin-eaters are ghostly magic and hollywood-style syncretic rituals and Fae are tricksy folk magic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T22:04:00-08:00","id":1181909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181843#post1181843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds good to me. Expand it to various Contract-like effects (as in focus on tricksiness rather than direct power) and it would be perfect, though now that contracts are no longer dot-rated, you'd have to figure out how to balance which level of favors get which contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Common Contracts are worth two or three dots of the old system, and Royal Contracts are worth 4 or 5. I'd have it so Minor Favour can get you a unique seeming bonus to modify a Common Contract you have, as a Medial Favour you can do the same for a Royal Contract, and as a Major Favour you can gain a Common Contract.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overlord62</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181848#post1181848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, while we\u2019re on the subject of changeling magic, I had this idea for two new merits called Hedge-speak and Wyrd-script. They would basically function like Mage\u2019s runes and high speach and provide bonuses to contracts like making them more powerful or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of thing is more handled by the loophole mechanic rather than bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-03-2018, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T22:05:35-08:00","id":1181910,"title":"","content":"Honestly... ignoring line themes (none of the splats are really &quot;chaotic&quot;), you could do worse than copying and pasting the 2e Awakening system. Throw away all the Practices and Arcana and come up with your own. Dawn, Day, Dusk, Night work fine as the latter (though having not seen DA:F, I don't really have a sense of what kinds of effects you're looking for and I'd expect you'd want more specific purviews), and you need a minimum of five Practices for the five dots in CofD's system. Most easily, the cantrip-like effects at the first dot, and &quot;unleashing&quot; at the fifth dot, and then span the distance. Use the same rough system for Paradox to get a sense of how badly things go wrong. Hard to name it when I don't have a sense for what you'd expect to happen when things go sideways. But instead of Reach, I'd suggest using Ante. You get none for free, ever, and when you want to push at what's possible, you up the Ante, dropping a bigger bet into the pot and hoping you don't muck out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T23:32:43-08:00","id":1181925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181910#post1181910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly... ignoring line themes (none of the splats are really &amp;quot;chaotic&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, you could do worse than copying and pasting the 2e Awakening system. Throw away all the Practices and Arcana and come up with your own. Dawn, Day, Dusk, Night work fine as the latter (though having not seen DA:F, I don't really have a sense of what kinds of effects you're looking for and I'd expect you'd want more specific purviews), and you need a minimum of five Practices for the five dots in CofD's system. Most easily, the cantrip-like effects at the first dot, and &amp;quot;unleashing&amp;quot; at the fifth dot, and then span the distance. Use the same rough system for Paradox to get a sense of how badly things go wrong. Hard to name it when I don't have a sense for what you'd expect to happen when things go sideways. But instead of Reach, I'd suggest using Ante. You get none for free, ever, and when you want to push at what's possible, you up the Ante, dropping a bigger bet into the pot and hoping you don't muck out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another model is Influences (as used by Spirits, Ghosts, etc.). You could even flavor it as the Changeling temporarily &quot;borrowing&quot; the use of it, or directly beseeching the facet of reality in question. Obviously the exact effect is up to the facet (read: Storyteller), so final results may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T17:32:33-08:00","id":1182443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overlord62</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings#post1181627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Changeling: The Lost but I was always a little disappointed that there wasn\u2019t a more flexible magic system. In Dark ages: Fae there was unleashing, which I thought was pretty cool and there are a few homebrew systems but they never really clicked with me. Do you guys have any ideas for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also something I've mulled over. I'm just not a fan of powersets made up of multiple small tricks, but something that just imitates the Arcana or Unleashing doesn't seem like it would fit.<br /> <br /> I think what I would do is expand the power and risk of Hedgespinning, which I might call <b>&quot;Inviting the Hedge&quot;</b>:<br /> <br /> If a changeling alters an environment in the mortal world to resemble the local Hedge, then with a boost of glamour they can take advantage of that closeness and engage in Hedgespinning as if they had crossed the border. The inherent risk would be that they're essentially making pieces of the Hedge and the mortal world overlap, with all of the potential problems one might imagine coming from that.<br /> <br /> <u>The less-extreme system hack:</u> Inviting the Hedge is just a feature bolted onto Hedgespinning, and using it accrues Goblin Debt like a Goblin Contract. The rest of Changeling's systems remain intact.<br /> <br /> <u>The more extreme system hack:</u> Hedgespinning (including Inviting the Hedge) becomes the main magic system. Contracts, instead of individual tricks, become traits rated 1-5 like in 1st edition, and they add to your dice pool when spinning effects in-theme. Trying to Invite the Hedge without the appropriate Contract, or failure on a roll, accrues Goblin Debt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T20:47:31-08:00","id":1182490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1182443#post1182443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...If a changeling alters an environment in the mortal world to resemble the local Hedge, then with a boost of glamour they can take advantage of that closeness and engage in Hedgespinning as if they had crossed the border. The inherent risk would be that they're essentially making pieces of the Hedge and the mortal world overlap, with all of the potential problems one might imagine coming from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds a lot like a Beast's ability to impose its Lair Traits on the waking world. It would be an interesting system to mess around with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T05:14:55-08:00","id":1182552,"title":"","content":"Sounds like it would be more situational though. You have to have enough thorny hedges, barbed wire fences, broken glass forests, sharp-leaved vines, etc to really get the feeling of the Hedge I'd say. But that could also encourage Earthbound Fae to create little Hedge-like sanctuaries for themselves deep in forgotten places, which is nicely thematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T06:14:59-08:00","id":1182889,"title":"","content":"I would really like to see David's 2E Goblin Contracts-like system to use for 'Sorcerers', like Autumn Courtiers- I seen that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> had some good ideas. Maybe you can expand it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T07:05:00-08:00","id":1183573,"title":"","content":"What is the 2E status of the Goblin Vow merit? Does anyone know if it will be included in one of the companions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T18:06:15-08:00","id":1183781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hedgebound Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1183573#post1183573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the 2E status of the Goblin Vow merit? Does anyone know if it will be included in one of the companions?</div> </div> </div> </div>There has been no official mention of it. It just was removed from Core and there hasn't been any dev comment on it's lack of appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T10:38:31-08:00","id":1184004,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I really enjoyed Goblin Vows, so hopefully they will be included at some point. I guess the David Hill version could be house ruled in the meantime. I have played around with kind of a &quot;quick and dirty&quot; version of Goblin Vows where the changeling doesn't need to worry about endeavors or sanctions and simply gives up dots of one Attribute, Skill, Merit, or Contract for a scene in order to get the same number of dots in a different one from the Goblin Vow's purview. Not only did the benefit gained need to be thematically appropriate for the purview, but it also needed to be the same type as what was given up(trading skills for skills or contracts for contracts, but no trading skills for contracts). The drawback was that in addition to gaining the benefit, the changeling also acquires a thematic frailty, condition, or tilt for the scene. It wasn't very elegant, but it worked in a pinch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T10:26:09-08:00","id":1185999,"title":"","content":"Does anyone remember <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/8978-wyrd-binding-expanded-goblin-vow-system\">Wyrd Binding</a>, the fan system of NeoTiamat for the previous Changeling the Lost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T12:40:54-08:00","id":1186042,"title":"","content":"It has been mentioned<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overlord62</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181627-flexible-magic-system-for-changelings?p=1181646#post1181646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">then there\u2019s wyrd-binding and I like the concept for it but it never really resonated with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T10:06:23-08:00","id":1187065,"title":"","content":"So, I just had a random thought... perhaps Goblin Vow could be reworked into a flat two-dot merit that has a single, specific purview. This merit can be purchased multiple times, but each purview must be unique. To use this merit, the changeling spends a point of Willpower in the presence of some representation of the purview to invoke an appropriately themed Goblin Contract(with the normal Glamour cost and dice pool). After this merit is traded for a contract, it disappears and the changeling now possesses the goblin contract that was used, with all of the usual benefits and drawbacks(while also satisfying Sanctity of Merits). I thought this would allow another option for greater flexibility, while staying mostly within the existing rules of the Second Edition Preview. Besides, I really like the idea of an Autumn Court sorcerer who carries around a seemingly random assortment of purview knickknacks and is always on the lookout to trade old contracts for new Goblin Vows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}